From: postmarketOS mojito port
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: arm-smmu-qcom: reserve hypervisor-owned context banks on qcs615

The hypervisor keeps context banks 10-12 and ignores S2CR writes that point a Linux stream at them,
so the ADSP audio stream 0x1721 never translated and the first ASM write crashed the DSP.
Patch 0017 of github.com/VipinVIP/violet-sm6150-mainline (MIT), unchanged.
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
index 0a6d45d75..2da83cc75 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -515,6 +515,18 @@ static int qcom_smmu_cfg_probe(struct arm_smmu_device *smmu)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * violet (sm6150/talos): the hypervisor keeps context banks 10-12 for its own streams and
+	 * silently ignores S2CR writes that point a Linux stream at them (the stream stays FAULT),
+	 * which is what stopped the ADSP audio stream 0x1721 from ever translating.  Hide them.
+	 */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(smmu->dev->of_node, "qcom,qcs615-smmu-500") &&
+	    smmu->num_context_banks > 12) {
+		set_bit(10, smmu->context_map);
+		set_bit(11, smmu->context_map);
+		set_bit(12, smmu->context_map);
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < smmu->num_mapping_groups; i++) {
 		smr = arm_smmu_gr0_read(smmu, ARM_SMMU_GR0_SMR(i));
 
